hey guys how we doing hope all is well  today I'd like to talk about a  conversation I've been seeing all over  the place recently which is the Eldon  Ring versus God of War Ragnarok Game of  the Year debate I don't really  understand the argument because  obviously stray is going to win no  question about it it's a cute cat game  but jokes aside I believe everyone's  sort of missing the point when having  this conversation in the first place now  obviously I'm a bit biased because this  channel is mainly Elden ring it's what  blew up my channel earlier this year so  yes it's my personal game of the year  I'm going to vote Elden ring as Game of  the Year it's opinion based it's a vote  so that means whichever game is your  favorite doesn't have to be Elden ring  or God of War you can vote for that game  without having to defend your opinion to  everybody if it was truly your favorite  game that you played this year then vote  for that and anyone giving you Flack for  voting for one game over another that  person probably has an unhealthy relay  relationship with the game that they  prefer but let's look at it from a  different perspective all of these games  are fantastic in their own unique ways  and obviously people are going to have  their own preferences Elden ring is a  massive open world game that tells you  nothing on the surface you have to read  tons of item descriptions to get the  deeper meaning to the overall story  there's no Quest markers and basically  nothing telling you where to go or what  to do besides this ominous glowing light  that more so leads you toward death than  the proper right direction and some  people don't like that some people like  to be told and shown the story at face  value they like Quest markers and lists  the check off and if you do prefer that  style of game you are going to love  every game on this list except for Elden  ring the main argument that I'm seeing  is that some people believe that Elden  ring doesn't have a story at all that's  right some people actually believe that  Elden ring has no narrative story three  whatsoever anyone who says that  obviously didn't pay enough attention  while playing the game because there is  a very simple narrative understanding of  the story of what you are trying to do  in Elden ring and they tell you all of  it from the very start of the game the  Elden ring has been broken and you are  summoned back to the lands between to  fix it that's your entire purpose fix  the Elden ring and become the Eldon Lord  and I'll tell you through my first  playthrough that is all I needed that  was my only objective was to become the  Elden Lord and I definitely didn't ask  why at any point now if you're trying to  understand the why to all of it that's  where you're gonna have to go down a  major Rabbit Hole to figure it all out  here's the thing if you're calling Elden  ring bad design for the way that they  made the story or the way they told the  story then you just don't understand  different types of narrative design in  video games and you're probably just  frustrated that you didn't right away  understand the entire story and you  would prefer if they just told you  everything at face value and I'm here to  tell you that thinking this way is  perfectly fine if it's your personal  preference to experience a story at face  value like Ragnarok then that's  obviously fine but if you're out there  saying to the world of Twitter or  whatever that Elden ring story is poorly  designed or that it barely has a story  to tell then you're a part of the reason  why this debate on Game of the Year is  stupid everything in Elden ring is  designed around a vague story completely  on purpose it is meant to leave you with  this feeling of uncertainty about  everything why did you do everything  you've done throughout the game what are  the true intentions of all of the  characters you met while playing the  game it's meant for all of us as a  community to come together and speculate  on what we think it all means and yes  the story is sometimes frustrating and  confusing that's why I like to take a  break from it from time to time to also  play games like stray and Ragnarok I  don't have to think about the story too  much and that's really nice that doesn't  take away from the creative genius of  Frome software's environmental  storytelling and like I said some people  hate that and that is perfectly fine  while on the flip side some people hate  being told where to go what to do how to  do it and what it all means Eldon ring  and Ragnarok completely succeeded 100 in  how they wanted to tell their own  individual stories Elden ring is meant  to be vague with a focus on  environmental storytelling while  Ragnarok is meant to be this Hollywood  style production that is meant to tell  you the story at face value and there is  nothing wrong with either of these  production Styles but I completely  understand why some people like and  dislike certain aspects of both of these  games that's where a vote comes in you  get to decide what your favorite gaming  experience was  whether your favorite game wins or not  whether Elden ring stray Ragnarok any of  the games whether they win it doesn't  really matter and honestly I didn't even  [ __ ] vote in 2020 or 2021 because I  didn't care about any of the games that  came out I've played the entirety of  Ragnarok since it came out and I can say  that there are some parts of Ragnarok  that I enjoy more than I did Elden ring  Ragnarok improved from the original in  2018 in basically every single way  Ragnarok is a very good game and just  because it's not exactly like Elden ring  doesn't mean I have to dislike it and  hate it I feel like a lot of people do  that and I I don't get it however I'm  picking Elden ring for game of the year  because first off it completely changed  my life it gave me a job creating  content for it that I absolutely love  it's a mental grind every single day  creating content if you're a content  creator out there you know what I'm  talking about it is very mentally taxing  but regardless I love doing it every  single day whether some days are a  struggle more than others whether it  Wins Game of the Year or not it doesn't  matter it was my game of the year I also  believe that eldenring as a whole has  made more of an impact on the gaming  industry than any other game has done in  recent memory it's basically this decade  Skyrim it's such a unique experience  compared to every other game on the  market with hundreds of hours of content  to consume that completely immersed me  into a beautifully constructed open  world and while Ragnarok improved off  its last iteration in 2018 it's  basically the same game from 2018 just  better eldenring took all of their past  games Demon Souls Dark Souls one two  three bloodborne sakuro and mix that all  together into a new IP that [ __ ] blew  my mind in February of this year both  games all the games on the game of the  year list for 2022 are awesome in their  own ways and I think what we all should  be talking about is what an amazing year  it was for gaming in general the last  few years have been complete butt cheeks  in terms of gaming most games coming out  being free to play filled with micro  transactions or they're completely  unfinished that needed months or even  years more of development to even be  close to finished Eldon ring and  Ragnarok said yeah we're not doing any  of that [ __ ] and they did what we all  really want as Gamers they just made a  good [ __ ] game it just feels good to  be a gamer right now I'm very happy  lately I was losing my love for gaming  for a little while there but this year  just completely revitalized all of my  love that I had for it Elden ring and  God of War Ragnarok should not only be  considered game of the year for 2022 but  should also be considered a couple of  the best games of all time for me Elden  ring takes that mantle for the best game  I've ever played for its influence on my  life in more ways than one thanks for  watching guys I hope you enjoyed this  new format another guy named Jake  standing in front of a green screen  right I just need an inflatable ball to  sit on and I'm basically naked Jakey I'm  still deep in the works with the fallen  leaves which is turning out to be a much  more major project than I anticipated  and it might take a little bit more time  than the end of November to get the  first episode done it's a lot of work  but I'm Gonna Keep at it and take my  time with it to make sure it's good  enough for me to give to you guys I'm  just really passionate about it so I  want to make sure I've done everything I  can to make it as good as it can be  before I release it but like I said I'm  not gonna rush it I'm just gonna take my  time until it gets done I'll be live  streaming the game awards on December  8th hopefully we get some Elden ring DLC  announcement with that as well that  would be really cool to see live that's  all I gotta say have a good one bye guys
 

